# server.env - where HQ and the game live. Public, no secrets. join.sh and crew.sh fetch this file fresh from GitHub
# (main) and fall back to the copy shipped with the lab (while the repo is private, the shipped copy decides).
#
# v7, the chosen HQ: every sandbox runs YOUR OWN HQ, a real Salt master inside the sandbox (solo.sh, 127.0.0.1 only),
# so the room needs no server, relay or presenter link. That is MODE=solo below: keep it in every copy (R119).
# The real Uyuni HQ runs on a GitHub-hosted runner (.github/workflows/hq.yml) for the stage and the HQ table only.
# Its address is new on every run, so this file holds the documented EXAMPLE until a run publishes the day's copy
# (hq.yml publish=true, lab/runner/server-env.sh), which reads:
#   FQDN=uyuni.<runner's own a-b-c-d>.sslip.io    HQ's own name; join.sh maps it to SERVER_IP in /etc/hosts
#   SERVER_IP=<the relay's IPv4>                 bore.pub's address; the relay serves exactly 4505/4506
#   RELAY=bore.pub
#   MODE=solo                                    the room stays on its own HQs whatever the address says
#   HQ_MASTER_FINGER_TAIL / HQ_MASTER_FINGER     that run's master key (a runner's key is new every run)
# The HQ table (Akash's sandbox + up to 7 front-table crews, CAP 8) joins the real HQ with: join.sh --hq
# Any HQ-table failure: join.sh --solo. Check a copy with: STRICT=1 bash lab/lint-server-env.sh attendee/server.env
# An empty GAME_URL switches the game off; the lab still works.
FQDN=uyuni.A-B-C-D.sslip.io
SERVER_IP=A.B.C.D
KEY=1-osas26-fleet
# The game's canonical origin: the Pages front (the QR code and the typed URL are the same host).
GAME_URL=https://geeko-hq.pages.dev
# Empty: a runner's master key is new on every run, so side quest F3 shows its no-tail text (G7g).
HQ_MASTER_FINGER_TAIL=
# Which HQ join.sh uses. solo = YOUR OWN HQ in every sandbox (the room, v7). hq = always the room's HQ.
# Empty = auto: the room's HQ when it answers on door 4506 within 6 s, else your own HQ.
MODE=solo
